       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day in a monitored setting. For OTC use the maximum is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also well above the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially. Normal renal and hepatic function doesn't offset that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for pain or fever\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is truly intended. If it is, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. I can then enter the order with a note about that discussion."
      }
